# Web/ (Next.js) settings. Copy to Web/.env.local only if you need one; most shops need none.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL (optional): a fixed address for the Express API, inlined into the pages
# at build time (rebuild after changing it).
#   Empty / unset (recommended for the shop): the browser calls the API on the same host it
#   opened the page from, port 5000, so the shop computer and LAN tablets just work.
#   Set it when the API lives elsewhere, e.g. AWS Amplify + a cloud API:
#     NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com
#   An https page cannot call an http API, so a cloud deployment needs an https API address.
#
# Never put DATABASE_URL, PG_LISTEN_URL, JWT_SECRET or TEST_DATABASE_URL here: they belong to
# Backend/.env only, and next.config.ts refuses to build or start if it sees them.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=
